{number: 103}
{title: Anywhere with Jesus}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Anywhere with Jesus I can safely go,
[G] Anywhere He leads me in this world be-[D] low;
Anywhere without Him dearest [A7] joys would fade,
[D] Anywhere with Jesus [A7] I am not a-[D] fraid.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Anywhere! Anywhere! [D] Fear I cannot know;
[A7] Anywhere with Jesus I can [D] safely go.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Anywhere with Jesus I need fear no ill,
[G] Tho' temptations gather round my pathway [D] still;
He Himself was tempted that He [A7] might help me;
[D] Anywhere with Jesus [A7] I may victor [D] be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] Anywhere with Jesus I am not alone;
[G] Other friends may fail me, He is still my [D] own;
Tho' His hand may lead me over [A7] dreary ways,
[D] Anywhere with Jesus [A7] is a house of [D] praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[D] Anywhere with Jesus I can go to sleep,
[G] When the dark'ning shadows round about me [D] creep;
Knowing I shall waken, never [A7] more to roam,
[D] Anywhere with Jesus [A7] will be home, sweet [D] home.
{end_of_verse}
